    {
      "id": 6,
      "line": [
        {"t": [0, 1, 2, 3], "es": "Vengan a conocerlos»."}
      ],
      "words": [
        {"t": [0], "es": "vengan", "base": "come", "sense": "move"},
        {"t": [1], "es": "y", "note": "Después de *come*, *and* une otra acción: *come and meet* equivale a «venir a conocer»."},
        {"t": [2], "es": "conozcan", "base": "meet", "sense": "introduction"},
        {"t": [3], "es": "los, a ellos"}
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 7,
      "line": [
        {"t": [0, 1, 2], "es": "El ministro del Gobierno"},
        {"t": [3, 4, 5, 6], "es": "era un hombre alto,"},
        {"t": [7, 8, 9, 10, 11], "es": "de cara alargada y delgada."}
      ],
      "words": [
        {"t": [0, 2], "es": "el ministro", "base": "minister", "sense": "government"},
        {"t": [1], "es": "del Gobierno", "base": "government", "sense": "authority", "note": "En *Government Minister*, el primer sustantivo describe al segundo: un ministro del Gobierno ([[noun-as-adjective]])."},
        {"t": [3], "es": "era", "base": "be", "sense": "identity"},
        {"t": [4, 6], "es": "un hombre", "base": "man", "sense": "adult"},
        {"t": [5], "es": "alto", "base": "tall", "sense": "height"},
        {"t": [7, 8, 11], "es": "con una cara", "base": "face", "sense": "front"},
        {"t": [9], "es": "larga, alargada", "base": "long", "sense": "length"},
        {"t": [10], "es": "delgada", "base": "thin", "sense": "body"}
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 8,
      "line": [
        {"t": [0, 1, 2, 3], "es": "Tenía el pelo rojizo"},
        {"t": [4, 5, 6, 7, 8], "es": "y una gran barba rojiza."}
      ],
      "words": [
        {"t": [0], "es": "él"},
        {"t": [1], "es": "tenía", "base": "have", "sense": "possess"},
        {"t": [2], "es": "rojizo", "base": "red", "sense": "hair", "note": "Con *hair*, *red* describe el pelo de una persona pelirroja, no un rojo vivo."},
        {"t": [3], "es": "pelo", "base": "hair", "sense": "growth"},
        {"t": [4], "es": "y"},
        {"t": [5, 8], "es": "una barba", "base": "beard", "sense": "facial-hair"},
        {"t": [6], "es": "grande", "base": "great", "sense": "large", "note": "Aquí *great* indica tamaño, no que algo sea estupendo."},
        {"t": [7], "es": "rojiza", "base": "red", "sense": "hair"}
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 9,
      "line": [
        {"t": [0, 1, 2, 3], "es": "Nos miró"},
        {"t": [4, 5, 6, 7], "es": "y no sonrió."}
      ],
      "words": [
        {"t": [0], "es": "él"},
        {"t": [1, 2], "es": "miró", "base": "look at", "sense": "watch", "note": "Para decir qué miras, se usa *look at*: no basta con *look*."},
        {"t": [3], "es": "nos, a nosotros"},
        {"t": [4], "es": "y"},
        {"t": [5, 6, 7], "es": "no sonrió", "base": "smile", "sense": "verb", "note": "*Did not* forma la negación en pasado. El verbo *smile* queda en su forma base ([[auxiliary-do]])."}
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 10,
      "line": [
        {"t": [0, 1, 2], "es": "A su lado"},
        {"t": [3, 4, 5], "es": "estaba de pie el señor Wilder,"},
        {"t": [6, 7, 8, 9], "es": "un hombre muy joven."}
      ],
      "words": [
        {"t": [0, 1], "es": "al lado de", "base": "next to", "sense": "beside"},
        {"t": [2], "es": "él"},
        {"t": [3], "es": "estaba de pie", "base": "stand", "sense": "upright", "note": "La frase empieza por el lugar, *next to him*, y el sujeto, *Mr Wilder*, va detrás del verbo ([[locative-inversion]])."},
        {"t": [4], "es": "señor", "note": "*Mr* va delante del apellido o del nombre completo. En inglés británico suele ir sin punto; en EE. UU., *Mr.* ([[british-american]])."},
        {"t": [5], "es": "Wilder"},
        {"t": [6, 9], "es": "un hombre", "base": "man", "sense": "adult"},
        {"t": [7], "es": "muy", "base": "very", "sense": "degree"},
        {"t": [8], "es": "joven", "base": "young", "sense": "age"}
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 11,
      "line": [
        {"t": [0, 1, 2], "es": "Era menudo,"},
        {"t": [3, 4, 5], "es": "de ojos azules"},
        {"t": [6, 7, 8, 9], "es": "y expresión vigilante."}
      ],
      "words": [
        {"t": [0], "es": "él"},
        {"t": [1], "es": "era", "base": "be", "sense": "identity"},
        {"t": [2], "es": "pequeño", "base": "small", "sense": "size"},
        {"t": [3, 5], "es": "con ojos", "base": "eye", "sense": "organ"},
        {"t": [4], "es": "azules", "base": "blue", "sense": "colour"},
        {"t": [6], "es": "y"},
        {"t": [7, 9], "es": "una cara", "base": "face", "sense": "front", "note": "*Face* puede indicar lo que expresa la cara. Por eso la frase dice «expresión»."},
        {"t": [8], "es": "vigilante, atenta", "base": "watchful", "sense": "alert"}
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 12,
      "line": [
        {"t": [0, 1, 2], "es": "Fue el primero en hablar."}
      ],
      "words": [
        {"t": [0], "es": "él"},
        {"t": [1], "es": "habló", "base": "speak", "sense": "talk"},
        {"t": [2], "es": "primero", "base": "first", "sense": "order"}
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 13,
      "line": [
        {"t": [0, 1, 2, 3], "es": "«Al duque le sorprende,"},
        {"t": [4, 5], "es": "doctor Huxtable,"},
        {"t": [6, 7, 8, 9, 10, 11], "es": "ver aquí al señor Sherlock Holmes."}
      ],
      "words": [
        {"t": [0, 1], "es": "el duque", "base": "duke", "sense": "noble"},
        {"t": [2], "es": "está", "base": "be", "sense": "state"},
        {"t": [3], "es": "sorprendido", "base": "surprised", "sense": "feeling"},
        {"t": [4], "es": "doctor", "note": "Abreviatura de *doctor*. En inglés británico suele ir sin punto; en EE. UU., *Dr.* ([[british-american]])."},
        {"t": [5], "es": "Huxtable"},
        {"t": [6, 7], "es": "ver", "base": "see", "sense": "sight", "note": "Tras *surprised*, el infinitivo con *to* dice qué causa la sorpresa: «sorprendido de ver», no «para ver» ([[adjective-infinitive]])."},
        {"t": [8], "es": "señor", "note": "*Mr* va delante del apellido o del nombre completo. En inglés británico suele ir sin punto; en EE. UU., *Mr.* ([[british-american]])."},
        {"t": [9, 10], "es": "Sherlock Holmes"},
        {"t": [11], "es": "aquí", "base": "here", "sense": "place"}
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 14,
      "line": [
        {"t": [0, 1, 2], "es": "No quiere"},
        {"t": [3, 4, 5, 6, 7], "es": "que la gente se entere de esto."}
      ],
      "words": [
        {"t": [0], "es": "él"},
        {"t": [1, 2], "es": "no quiere", "base": "want", "sense": "desire", "note": "*Doesn’t* es *does not* ([[contractions]]). Para negar con *he*, se usa *does not* y el verbo en forma base ([[auxiliary-do]])."},
        {"t": [3], "es": "gente, personas", "base": "person", "sense": "human", "note": "*People* es el plural de *person*. Lleva verbo en plural, aunque «gente» sea singular ([[plural-agreement]])."},
        {"t": [4, 5, 6], "es": "saber de", "base": "know", "sense": "information", "note": "Con *want*, el sujeto del infinitivo va delante de *to*: *want people to know* = «querer que la gente sepa» ([[object-infinitive]])."},
        {"t": [7], "es": "esto"}
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 15,
      "line": [
        {"t": [0, 1, 2, 3], "es": "Usted lo sabe, así que"},
        {"t": [4, 5, 6, 7, 8, 9, 10], "es": "¿por qué no habló con el duque"},
        {"t": [11, 12, 13, 14, 15], "es": "antes de ir a Londres?»."}
      ],
      "words": [
        {"t": [0], "es": "usted"},
        {"t": [1], "es": "sabe", "base": "know", "sense": "information"},
        {"t": [2], "es": "eso"},
        {"t": [3], "es": "así que", "base": "so", "sense": "result"},
        {"t": [4], "es": "por qué", "base": "why", "sense": "question"},
        {"t": [5, 7, 8], "es": "no habló con", "base": "speak", "sense": "talk", "note": "*Didn’t* es *did not* ([[contractions]]). En la pregunta va antes del sujeto, y *speak* queda en forma base ([[auxiliary-do]])."},
        {"t": [6], "es": "usted"},
        {"t": [9, 10], "es": "el duque", "base": "duke", "sense": "noble"},
        {"t": [11], "es": "antes de que", "base": "before", "sense": "earlier-than"},
        {"t": [12], "es": "usted"},
        {"t": [13], "es": "fue", "base": "go", "sense": "move"},
        {"t": [14, 15], "es": "a Londres"}
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 16,
      "line": [
        {"t": [0, 1, 2, 3], "es": "«Pero necesitamos ayuda»,"},
        {"t": [4, 5, 6], "es": "dijo el doctor Huxtable."}
